Rule 1 (input tensor dtype must be one of the supported indices 0–11)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 11
>>
Rule 2 (rank of the input tensor is non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 0 ≤ ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 3 (scalar tensor has a degenerate range)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then min(v_1) = max(v_1)
>>
Rule 4 (boolean tensor values are within {0,1})
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 0 then min(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 1
>>
Rule 5 (integer tensor has an ordered range)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5 then min(v_1) ≤ max(v_1)
>>
Rule 6 (floating tensor has a non-negative span)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 then max(v_1) - min(v_1) ≥ 0
